(RESERVE BANK OF INDIA) Tj
T*
(FINANCIAL INCLUSION AND DEVELOPMENT DEPARTMENT, MUMBAI) Tj
T*
(RBI/2024-25/140 FIDD.CO.Plan.BC.5/04.09.01/2024-25) Tj
T*
(September 25, 2024) Tj
T*
(Master Direction - Priority Sector Lending \(PSL\) Targets and Classification) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Overall PSL Target: Domestic commercial banks \(excluding Regional Rural Banks and Small Finance Banks\) and foreign banks with 20) Tj
T*
(branches and above shall achieve an overall Priority Sector Lending target of 40 percent of Adjusted Net Bank Credit \(ANBC\) or Credit) Tj
T*
(Equivalent Amount of Off-Balance Sheet Exposure \(CEOBE\), whichever is higher.) Tj
T*
(2. Agriculture Sub-target: Within the overall PSL target, a sub-target of 18 percent of ANBC or CEOBE is mandated for Agriculture.) Tj
T*
(Out of the 18 percent allocated to agriculture, a sub-target of 10 percent of ANBC is specifically earmarked for Small and Marginal) Tj
T*
(Farmers \(SMFs\).) Tj
T*
(3. Micro Enterprises Target: A sub-target of 7.5 percent of ANBC or CEOBE is prescribed for advances to Micro Enterprises under the) Tj
T*
(Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises Development \(MSMED\) Act, 2006.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
9 0 obj
<< /Length 998 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 720 Td
13 TL
(4. Weaker Sections Sub-target: The target for advances to Weaker Sections is set at 12 percent of ANBC or CEOBE.) Tj
T*
(Beneficiaries classified under Weaker Sections include small and marginal farmers, artisans, Scheduled Castes and Scheduled Tribes,) Tj
T*
(women borrowers up to rupees one lakh, and beneficiaries of Differential Rate of Interest \(DRI\) schemes.) Tj
T*
(5. Foreign Banks with Less Than 20 Branches: Foreign banks with less than 20 branches have an overall Priority Sector Lending target) Tj
T*
(of 40 percent of ANBC or CEOBE, with no specific sub-targets for agriculture or micro enterprises, provided that not less than 32 percent) Tj
T*
(is in the form of export credit.) Tj
T*
(6. Shortfall Penalty: Banks having any shortfall in achievement of PSL targets shall be required to contribute to the Rural Infrastructure) Tj
T*
(Development Fund \(RIDF\) established with NABARD or other designated funds as decided by the Reserve Bank.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
10 0 obj
<< /Length 967 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 720 Td
13 TL
(7. Clean Energy and Renewable Projects: Bank loans up to a limit of rupees thirty crore \(INR 30,00,00,000\) to borrowers for) Tj
T*
(solar-based power generators, biomass power plants, wind mills, and micro-hydel plants are eligible for classification under Priority) Tj
T*
(Sector Lending. For individual households, the loan limit is rupees ten lakh per borrower.) Tj
T*
(8. Social Infrastructure Limits: Bank loans up to a limit of rupees five crore \(INR 5,00,00,000\) per borrower for setting up schools,) Tj
T*
(drinking water facilities, and sanitation facilities in Tier II to Tier VI centres are classified under PSL.) Tj
T*
(9. Housing Loan Limits: Loans to individuals up to rupees thirty-five lakh in metropolitan centres \(population 10 lakh and above\) and) Tj
T*
(up to rupees twenty-five lakh in other centres are eligible for PSL classification, provided dwelling unit costs do not exceed prescribed ceilings.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
